The Regular Polygon's Two Faces — opus-S528

======================================================================
PART 1: Regular polygon — boundary vs diagonals
======================================================================

n=4:
  total edges: C(4,2) = 6
  boundary (d=1): 4
  diagonals (d≥2): 2
  inside/outside ratio: 2/4 = 0.50

  by diagonal length d:
    d=1: 4 edges — boundary
    d=2: 2 edges — half-turn boundary
  observer's edges: 2 boundary + 1 diagonals
  at regular polygon: all distances = d/n ≥ 1/4 → observer is SOURCE

n=5:
  total edges: C(5,2) = 10
  boundary (d=1): 5
  diagonals (d≥2): 5
  inside/outside ratio: 5/5 = 1.00

  by diagonal length d:
    d=1: 5 edges — boundary
    d=2: 5 edges — aligned
  observer's edges: 2 boundary + 2 diagonals
  at regular polygon: all distances = d/n ≥ 1/5 → observer is SOURCE

n=6:
  total edges: C(6,2) = 15
  boundary (d=1): 6
  diagonals (d≥2): 9
  inside/outside ratio: 9/6 = 1.50

  by diagonal length d:
    d=1: 6 edges — boundary
    d=2: 6 edges — aligned
    d=3: 3 edges — half-turn boundary
  observer's edges: 2 boundary + 3 diagonals
  at regular polygon: all distances = d/n ≥ 1/6 → observer is SOURCE

n=7:
  total edges: C(7,2) = 21
  boundary (d=1): 7
  diagonals (d≥2): 14
  inside/outside ratio: 14/7 = 2.00

  by diagonal length d:
    d=1: 7 edges — boundary
    d=2: 7 edges — aligned
    d=3: 7 edges — aligned
  observer's edges: 2 boundary + 4 diagonals
  at regular polygon: all distances = d/n ≥ 1/7 → observer is SOURCE

n=8:
  total edges: C(8,2) = 28
  boundary (d=1): 8
  diagonals (d≥2): 20
  inside/outside ratio: 20/8 = 2.50

  by diagonal length d:
    d=1: 8 edges — boundary
    d=2: 8 edges — aligned
    d=3: 8 edges — aligned
    d=4: 4 edges — half-turn boundary
  observer's edges: 2 boundary + 5 diagonals
  at regular polygon: all distances = d/n ≥ 1/8 → observer is SOURCE

n=14:
  total edges: C(14,2) = 91
  boundary (d=1): 14
  diagonals (d≥2): 77
  inside/outside ratio: 77/14 = 5.50

  by diagonal length d:
    d=1: 14 edges — boundary
    d=2: 14 edges — aligned
    d=3: 14 edges — aligned
    d=4: 14 edges — aligned
    d=5: 14 edges — aligned
    d=6: 14 edges — aligned
    d=7: 7 edges — half-turn boundary
  observer's edges: 2 boundary + 11 diagonals
  at regular polygon: all distances = d/n ≥ 1/14 → observer is SOURCE

THE INSIDE/OUTSIDE RATIO:
  n=4: 2.0  (2 diagonals per boundary edge)
  n=6: 3.0  (3:1)
  n=7: 3.5  (3.5:1)
  n=14: 10.0 (10:1)

  The CASCADE works when inside >> outside:
  enough hidden degrees of freedom to force the visible state.
  The transition is at n=7 (ratio 3.5) — the inside just barely
  dominates the outside.

