PART 5: The walk — inside flips driving outside changes
======================================================================

n=5 (initial segment):
  total walls: 40
  inside (diagonal) walls: 14 (35%)
  outside (boundary) walls: 26 (65%)
  average inside run between outside walls: 0.5
  max inside run: 6
  obs outdeg at outside walls: Counter({3: 12, 4: 8, 2: 4, 1: 2})

n=7 (initial segment):
  total walls: 112
  inside (diagonal) walls: 55 (49%)
  outside (boundary) walls: 57 (51%)
  average inside run between outside walls: 1.0
  max inside run: 15
  obs outdeg at outside walls: Counter({5: 28, 6: 12, 4: 8, 3: 5, 1: 2, 2: 2})

THE PICTURE: the walk is mostly INSIDE diagonal flips
(changing the hidden tournament class) punctuated by
occasional OUTSIDE boundary flips (changing observer's status).

The inside flips ACCUMULATE, shifting the tournament through
metagraph classes, until the accumulated change forces an
outside flip that pushes the observer toward source.

This is the MECHANISM of the cascade:
  1. The inside has more edges than the outside (richness > 1)
